# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Pick ONE of the options below. They are checked in this order.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Option 1 (recommended for deployed sites): use the serverless proxy in /api/tmdb.ts.
# The real token stays on the server. Set TMDB_READ_TOKEN in your Vercel
# project settings (NOT prefixed with VITE_), and point the client at the proxy:
VITE_TMDB_PROXY_URL=/api/tmdb
# TMDB_READ_TOKEN=your_v4_read_access_token   <- server only (Vercel env / .env for `vercel dev`)

# Option 2 (local development): TMDB v4 "API Read Access Token", sent as a Bearer header.
# VITE_TMDB_READ_TOKEN=your_v4_read_access_token

# Option 3 (legacy): v3 API key. Works, but ends up in the URL query string.
# VITE_TMDB_API_KEY=your_v3_api_key
